// THE IN-SEASON FREE AGENT POOL -- the ranked board behind /free-agency.
//
// GENERATED, NOT WRITTEN. These rows come from EDFL_FreeAgentPool_Top150_2026-09-08.json,
// which was itself produced chat-side against the live database by
// EDFL_FreeAgentPool_Top150_rebuild.sql (a read-only query kept outside this repo, per
// ground rule 2). Do not hand-edit a row. To refresh -- a new Player Value Chart snapshot,
// or the 2025 results republished -- re-run the rebuild query chat-side and regenerate this
// file from the new JSON. The field list below is the contract; the generator selects
// exactly these keys and nothing else.
//
// THIS FILE CARRIES ONLY THE SLOW-MOVING FACTS. Rank, chart tier and PPV, and published
// 2025 production change when a chart is published or a season is republished, which is
// rarely. Everything time-sensitive is deliberately ABSENT so it can never be rendered
// stale:
//   - who is still available     -> decided at request time against `contracts`
//   - whether the first valid offer wins him (5.14(b)) -> derived live from the same read
//   - acquisition_path / first_offer_exempt / has_prior_contract / nfl_status -> stripped
//   - nfl_team                   -> PRESENT IN THIS FILE AND DELIBERATELY NOT DRAWN. It
//                                   was filed as slow-moving and is not: eighteen of the
//                                   150 rows below were wrong within five days. Since
//                                   September 13 2026 loadFreeAgencyState() overwrites it
//                                   from `players` on every render. Leave the key in the
//                                   generator contract -- it is useful when regenerating
//                                   and diffing -- but never render it.
// A player signed ten minutes after this list was built drops off the board on the next
// render because the page inner-joins these rows against the live contract index. See
// loadFreeAgencyState() in app/free-agency/actions.js.
//
// THE RANKING IS A DISCOVERY AID, NOT A PRICE LIST, and the owners know the ordering is
// subjective (commissioner, Sep 8 2026). Nothing here authorises an offer; every rule is
// tested by submit_fa_offer(), and chart_bid_target() in the database remains the
// authority on what an offer should be. per_year_value and likely_years are kept for
// completeness but the board does not draw them as a price column for that reason.
//
// HOW THE 150 WERE RANKED (commissioner rulings, Sep 8 2026):
//   blend      = 0.50 * ppv_index + 0.50 * prod_index
//   ppv_index  = 100 * total_ppv / (highest total_ppv in the candidate pool), league-wide;
//                off the chart = 0
//   prod_index = percentile rank of the 2025 composite among candidate-pool players at the
//                SAME position, 0-100; composite = 0.75 * points + 0.25 * (FPPG * 17)
//   selection  = positional floors (QB 12 / RB 28 / WR 40 / TE 22 / K 12) + 36 by blend
// `rank` is a rough cross-positional ordering; `position_rank` is the number the list is
// actually good at. Ties: blend, then total_ppv, then composite, then name.
//
// ELIGIBILITY AT BUILD TIME was edfl_free_agent_eligible(), the built function, not the
// spec text -- it rules in-season-released players eligible, which is why Zach Charbonnet
// is rank 4. Every row has a non-null sleeper_player_id; that filter is what keeps the
// 62 split-identity orphan rows (see CLAUDE.md) out of the pool.
//
// production_from_stats_twin_row = true means the player's 2025 figures were recovered
// from a duplicate players row under a suffixed spelling of his name. Seven rows carry it.
// A player whose two rows do not name-match shows the same has_2025_results = true here
// only if his own row had a result; the residual understatement is bounded and visible.

